所以我鼓励你去和 Codex 或者 Claude 聊聊，你可以问它：我在这里可以做哪些实验？
So I encourage you to just go talk to Codex or a cloud Code, you can tell it, which kind of experiments can I do here?

448
00:43:31,056 --> 00:43:40,548
不要太担心规模问题。我只是想让你学会如何做一些实验，学习科学思维，如何正确测量，以及如何得出结论。
And don't be so concerned about scaling. I just want you to learn how to do some experiments, how to learn scientific thinking, how to measure properly, how to conclude properly.

449
00:43:40,942 --> 00:43:43,616
你也可以把你的实验发到社交媒体上。
So you can post your experiments on social media as well.

450
00:43:43,854 --> 00:43:50,404
如果你想成为 AI 研究员，我建议你坚持每天或每周在社交媒体上发布你的实验。
If you want to become AI researcher, I recommend you just keep posting your experiments every day or every week on social media.

451
00:43:50,958 --> 00:43:53,828
持续性比强度更重要。
Consistency is more important than intensity.

452
00:43:54,606 --> 00:44:01,476
如果你连续发了五天然后就停了，那效果就不好；如果每周坚持发一次，一直坚持下去，效果要好得多。
So if you post five days in a row but then you stop, it's not good. If you post once a week, forever, it's a lot better.

453
00:44:02,318 --> 00:44:07,876
而且最好是去做实验，哪怕只是训练几秒钟的模型也好。
And it's better to just do experiments and train a model for a few seconds.

454
00:44:08,174 --> 00:44:17,616
你不想浪费时间去等待几分钟或几个小时。你需要思考并练习如何设计实验、环境和问题。
You don't want to wait a few minutes, a few hours because it's wasted time. You need to be thinking how to need to be practicing how to design experiments, environments, questions.

455
00:44:17,902 --> 00:44:24,772
你没必要去等模型，因为你不可能训练出一个能和那些大公司竞争、让大众使用的模型。
You don't need to wait for the model because you cannot train a model that's gonna outcompete these companies that people are gonna use.

